Alanna ran $d$ kilometers at an average speed of $v$ kilometers per hour, so it took her $\dfrac dv$ hours:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{\left(d\,\text{kilometers}\right)}{\left(v\,\dfrac{\text{kilometers}}{\text{hour}}\right)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac dv\,\cancel{\text{kilometers}}\cdot\dfrac{\text{hours}}{\cancel{\text{kilometer}}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac dv\,\text{hours}
\end{align}$
